  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​809 — November 3, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192358/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0 12px;\"><p>JavaScript Weekly</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192302/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/dhcgdjewfv50joacutkm.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>The AI Cost of JavaScript Frameworks</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192302/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Nolan Lawson had Claude build the same app</a> five times in each of twelve JS stacks to test common <em>\"X is better for agents\"</em> claims. Costs varied significantly between runs, and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192303/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Gautam Parab found</a> that the observed cost ranges overlapped or touched for most pairs of frameworks.</p>\n<p>But a clearer difference was in the median amount of JavaScript sent to browsers: 0KB for Astro, 18K for Hono+htmx, 36K for SvelteKit, and 115–142K for React Router, TanStack Start and Next.js. If you've gone \"hands-free\", Nolan asks, why stick to a particular stack you chose when you wrote all the code? <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192304/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">His benchmark</a> is on GitHub to try for yourself.</p>\n<p>Nolan Lawson</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192301/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"130\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/3575e54e.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"130\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192301/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"master.dev\">Run AI Coding Models on Your Own Machine</a></span> — Local models are now good enough for everyday coding. Learn to run them on your own Mac or GPU, wire them into your editor and terminal agents, and keep your code private with no per-token bill.</p>\n<p>Master.dev <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192305/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nullpt.rs\">Why Is This Fingerprinting Script 'Creating Bioweapons'?</a></span> — A crawl of sites to collect canvas fingerprinting examples (which you can see, visually, at <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192306/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">fingerprint.garden</a>) found an anti-analysis technique where JavaScript identifiers were named after… <em>taboo</em> topics, with a prompt hidden in invisible Unicode, all designed to make LLMs refuse to work on the code!</p>\n<p>Veritas </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 Canvas fingerprinting is a technique that uses quirks of how different clients render canvas elements, in order to <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192307/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">distinguish browser environments</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>😄 Bartosz shares <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192308/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">a creative way to generate strings and run code</a> without parentheses or quotes. Good old JavaScript fun!</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📊 GitHub's <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192309/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Octoverse 2026 report</a> has TypeScript as the most used language on GitHub by contributors (with JS at third), and ~44% of merged TypeScript PRs showing AI involvement. Plus a lot more besides.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>GitHub Actions will <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192310/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">block <code>pull_request_target</code> by default in public repos</a> from December 2, unless an event policy explicitly allows it, with brownouts on November 9 &amp; 16.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Cloudflare Workers now <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192311/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">supports the Temporal API natively</a> behind a <code>temporal</code> compatibility flag. It'll be available by default from December 1.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>RELEASES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192312/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js v27.0 (Alpha)</a> and <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192313/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">v26.13.0 (LTS)</a> – Node 26 is now the 'Lithium' LTS line, and 27 is the first ever Node 'alpha'. Under Node's new <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192314/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">release process</a>, every line spends six months in alpha before going <em>Current</em>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192315/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Vitest 5.1</a> – A new <code>--since-last-run</code> flag reruns only tests affected by your edits, plus there's an interactive snapshot review feature.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192316/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Rspack 2.3</a> – The Rust-based webpack alternative adopts <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192317/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">SWC Next</a> and its rewritten parser. The team reports 5-20% faster builds and less peak memory use.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192318/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Leaflet 2.0 Beta 1</a> – The mapping library's first major in a decade goes tree-shakeable, ships TypeScript types, and drops its default export.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192319/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Effect 4.1</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192320/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">pnpm 12.17</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192321/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">ESLint 10.14.0</a>, <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192322/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Nuxt DevTools v4</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📖  Articles and Videos</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192323/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/jz81mfwsiw9cmfmuz7qi.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192323/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"smoores.dev\">\"<em>No, npm, 'estee' is not a typo of 'testem'</em>\"</a></span> — Shane tried to publish a CLI called <code>estee</code> and hit npm's typosquatting filter, which (as best as we can tell) rejects names within a small <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192324/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Levenshtein distance</a> of popular packages' names.</p>\n<p>Shane Friedman </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192325/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"clarity.microsoft.com\">Shrinking <code>clarity.js</code>: When Cleaner Code Gzips Worse</a></span> — Microsoft let an agent run 50+ size experiments on its analytics script. A big win came from dropping <code>import *</code> namespace objects, while good-practice refactors like extracting helpers actually made the gzipped output <em>bigger</em>.</p>\n<p>Manu Nair (Microsoft) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192326/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"sentry.io\">Workshop: How to Implement Session Replay</a></span> — Filters, custom tags, and sampling settings for finding the sessions that matter. Nov 5, 10am PT.</p>\n<p>Sentry <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192327/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"brunoj.com\">'Nothing Installs at Our Company Until It's a Week Old'</a></span> — Many recent package hijacks were caught within hours, so Bruno's company now makes new releases wait a week. He explains what this approach broke, what cooldowns don't stop, and settings for popular package managers.</p>\n<p>Bruno Jurković </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192328/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"denodell.com\">Timing Ten Design Systems, Then Fixing the Slow Ones</a></span> — Den timed ten design systems (MUI, Ant Design, and Ionic among them) opening a 249-option select and ticking 100 checkboxes, then profiled the slow ones to find out why.</p>\n<p>Den Odell </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192329/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"charpeni.com\">Using Bun? Dependabot Can't See Most of Your Dependencies</a></span> — GitHub's dependency graph doesn't parse <code>bun.lock</code>, so Dependabot alerts cover only direct dependencies. Nicolas has some tips for improving matters.</p>\n<p>Nicolas Charpentier (Shortcut) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192330/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">How Hard Is It to Check for Whitespace?</a> – Why Java, Python and JavaScript disagree on what counts as whitespace. <cite>Sergey Tselovalnikov</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192331/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">A Proposal: How to Hire Junior Engineers in the Age of AI</a> – The npm co-founder thinks traditional coding interviews are dead. <cite>Laurie Voss</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192332/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">How to Make <code>postMessage</code> Type-Safe in Under 350 Bytes</a> <cite>Pavel Grinchenko (Evil Martians)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192333/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">The Web Can't Afford a JavaScript Runtime Monoculture</a> <cite>Kate Holterhoff (RedMonk)</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192334/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/mwjj3fo3dcfpooypxjfz.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192334/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"chenglou.me\">Handwired: Compile Regular JavaScript into a Neural Net</a></span> — A new mind-bender from <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192335/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Pretext</a>'s creator: a compiler that turns JavaScript into an exact network of ReLUs and matrix multiplies that run on the GPU. Demos include a 130-layer 'mini desktop' and a WebGPU search over 100K JSON documents.</p>\n<p>Cheng Lou </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192339/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"serpapi.com\">Build Smarter JavaScript Applications With Live Search Data</a></span> — Add search, shopping, maps, news, trends, flights and hotels results with a single developer-friendly JavaScript SDK.</p>\n<p>SerpApi <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>🌐</span> <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192337/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"x18n.dev\">x18n: Lint and Maintain i18n Files for Any Framework</a></span> — Anthony Fu's successor to <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192338/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">i18n-ally</a> scans locale files and translation calls and reports missing, unused and broken keys (like how <code>tsc --noEmit</code> reports type errors).</p>\n<p>Anthony Fu </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192340/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">djs: A New 'Suspend Anywhere' JavaScript Engine</a></span> — Armin (of <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192341/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Flask</a> fame) built an engine to run scripts in WebAssembly that can snapshot the VM's state and resume elsewhere, even mid-<code>await</code>.</p>\n<p>Armin Ronacher </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192342/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">webframe: Run a Web Page Like a Command-Line Program</a></span> — Point it at a URL or HTML file and it runs the page in a hidden system web view, piping <code>console.log()</code> to stdout and exceptions to stderr. No bundled browser or Playwright needed.</p>\n<p>Jeff Lindsay </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192343/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/habczwydrpwycxp8usru.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192343/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"kevs3d.co.uk\">phoria2: A Small WebGL 2 Library for 3D Charts</a></span> — A dependency-free 3D library aimed at dashboards and product viewers, with an API you can 'learn in an afternoon'. Plenty of live demos on the page.</p>\n<p>Kevin Roast </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192344/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Shiki 4.6</a> – Powerful code syntax highlighter, now with faster decoration handling and compressed Oniguruma WASM binary.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192345/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Preact 11.1</a> – A new <code>preact/compat/compiler-runtime</code> entry point lets code compiled by React Compiler run on Preact too.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192346/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Postgres.js 4.0</a> – The popular Postgres client for Node, Bun and Cloudflare Workers gets a rewrite and goes ESM-only.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>💸 Every OTP you send costs money. Fraudsters trigger them by the thousands. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192348/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Fingerprint</a> recognizes the device before you text. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192348/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Learn how</a>.</p>\n<p>Your coding agent can write the app. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192349/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo</a> is the agentic mobile infrastructure that takes it from a repo to the App Store.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192350/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">CodeAF</a> fixed 2x OpenCode's issues and nearly 4x Claude Code's on the same open model, at up to 4.8x less per fix. Open source, Apache 2.0.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192351/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/puujepssorqipappmqpg.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Chrome 157 is due today with the headline feature being <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192351/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">HTML-in-Canvas</a> for drawing live, interactive DOM elements into 2D, WebGL and WebGPU canvases. This feature has <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192352/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">numerous striking applications</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>☕ <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192353/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">CheerpJ 5.0</a> brings Java 21 and 25 to the browser via WebAssembly, ships the full JDK so you can compile Java in a tab, and previews a new WasmGC-based engine the team hopes will run Minecraft and IntelliJ one day.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🤖 LLM-whisperer Simon Willison <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192354/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">looks at the world of browser games being built with coding agents</a>, and argues October was the point where agents got good enough to ship playable games.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🕹️ Talking of games… GitHub's game jam <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192355/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Game Off</em> is back for its 14th year</a> with the theme 'SHIFT'. Entries are due on <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192356/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">itch.io</a> by December 1.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
